            <ArticleTitle>Left ventricular-coronary sinus fistula after mitral valve replacement: case report and ultrafast CT findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Postoperative fistula from left ventricle to right atrium is a rare complication of mitral valve surgery. We describe a case identified by ultrafast computed tomography (CT) and we review the literature regarding this entity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
